CONFORMANCE.md §2.2: a String method and a call of a function that is not exported.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Twice x.
fn twice(x: Int) -> Int { return x * 2 }

/// A score.
export fn score(name: String, n: Int) -> Int { return name.len() + twice(n) }

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E9001]  a/a.canon:7:55
  name.len() is not allowed in translated function score: it is outside the portable subset; compute it at build time, in an export fn over finite parameters that this function calls, or keep that logic out of translated functions

error[E9001]  a/a.canon:7:68
  twice(n) is not allowed in translated function score: it is outside the portable subset; compute it at build time, in an export fn over finite parameters that this function calls, or keep that logic out of translated functions

